%% Prospective design before implementation. Separate physical jobs, not a proven runtime lineage.
flowchart TD
    Player[Player opens Army needs] --> Panel[Scene-owned ArmySupplyPanel]
    Session[Current GameSession] -->|committed state / replacement| Dirty[Dirty visible presentation]
    Intent[RearLogistics intent owner] -->|changed| Dirty
    Panel -->|shown| Dirty
    Dirty --> Coalesce[One deferred visible refresh; no idle timer or frame polling]
    Coalesce --> Query[Pure ArmySupplyView.view of current session]
    Query --> Need[Reported rifle requests + actual carried rounds + courier commitments]
    Query --> Stock[Available rear / HQ / forward stock]
    Query --> Trips[Actual separate rear and forward job quantities and blockers]
    Query --> Hold[Owner-provided cancellation hold]
    Need --> Display[Need, physical stages, blockers and useful existing actions]
    Stock --> Display
    Trips --> Display
    Hold --> Display
    Display -->|production / building / workers / rear requests| Existing[Existing exact controls; retain drafts]
    Display -->|observe selected friendly recipient| Observe[Existing battlefield observation; no tactical command]
    Display -->|explicit resume automatic supply| Resume[RearLogistics.resume_automatic_supply]
    Resume --> Clear[Clear only cancellation intent and invalidate published need]
    Clear --> Next[Next owned military resupply event recomputes genuine shortage]
    Next --> Demand[Existing rear_supply_needed event]
    Demand --> Intent
    Intent --> Physical[Existing real hauling, loading, travel, HQ unload]
    Physical --> Forward[Existing military forward freight and local issue]
    Forward --> Need
    Session -->|replacement / panel exit| Disconnect[Disconnect old subscriptions and reject stale work]
